  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "中西文學跨域解讀(一)",
    "sub_ename": "INTERDISCIPLINARY READINGS IN CHINESE AND WESTERN LITERATURE(1)",
    "describe_ch": "本課程將以編年體的方式，來介紹中古時期到十八世紀間西方文學中的重要作品。在過程中，將透過閱讀經典英美文學文本，來說明歷史、文體、作品、以及作者間的多重關係。再者，亦將透過介紹對應的經典中國文學作品，來解讀中西作者們，如何透過書寫來針對相同主題，表達其人文關懷。並且進一步的去了解這樣的文學表現，如何呈現出中西文化的共通性以及獨特性。",
    "describe_eh": "This course adopts a chronological approach to introduce major works in English and American literature from the medieval time to the eighteenth century. Through close readings of classic literary texts, it explores the complex relationships among history, literary genres, works, and authors. In addition, by engaging with corresponding masterpieces from Chinese literature, the course also examines how Western and Chinese canonical writers address similar themes with their distinct expressions of humanistic concerns. Such investigations will reveal the shared and unique characteristics between Western and Chinese cultures.",
    "pre_subname": "",
